    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like a solid starting point. I'm particularly concerned about the 'veneer of normalcy' when it comes to timestamps and packet sizing. If the oversight agencies see bursts of unusual activity at odd hours, they'll start digging. Can you suggest a specific way to stagger the transmission intervals or vary the data payloads so they look like natural, automated system updates or routine administrative backups instead of manual, high-priority messages?",
